<p>Not quite. The cars they sold in 2007 were the 2008 year model, and were made in 2008. In 2008, they receive the 2009 year model cars from the future, but are unable to sell enough of them to make a profit due to the global recession. However, they still have to make the cars in 2009 to send back to 2008, because otherwise, where did the cars they got in 2008 come from? They end up making all of the 2009 year model cars and send them back in time, but go bankrupt in the process.</p>

